no input port (`HasInputGrip`); (f) a value list's value text is its first selected item's name; (g) `CanvasReader.Health` and `ToLevel` are public additions for Chunk 04's `status`. Of these, (a) is the one a later wave depends on and is worth one line in C1.8.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/ObjectResolver.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/CanvasSnapshot.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/CanvasReader.cs"], "oid": "O-22"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Three goals still marked inferred are built into the keystone resolver", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The plan's Goals mark these as inferences, not owner rulings, and Chunk 01 fixes each in `ObjectResolver`: names are scoped and ids are not (a GUID or prefix reaches a group from an object action; a name never crosses scope); matching is exact, ordinal, case-sensitive and untrimmed; a default nickname resolves when unique, on destructive actions too. The third is the plan's one flagged owner's call, to be shown in the PR, and the plan states its reversal cost (one condition in the resolver plus tests). Chunks 02 and 04 build on all three, so the cost of a different answer rises with each merge; the PR is currently the only place the owner sees them.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/ObjectResolver.cs"], "oid": "O-23"}, {"goal": "Records Pass", "title": "Records Pass: both oracle files read; the plan clears no bar; the uncommitted Stats contribution row could not be corroborated", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Set covered: `.prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-canvas-read.md` and `.prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md`. The plan: C1's amended text agrees with the code on every point checked, the Chunk 01 deliverable list is one revision short in two places (it still says a group's pivot and a Names read without type names) and the decisions section carries the truth for the first; neither would send the Chunk 02 or 04 delegate the wrong way, so no finding. The preferences file: the on